        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Paul Sartre, George Bernard Shaw\n- Works: Nausea\n- Roles: philosopher, playwright, novelist, political activist, biographer, literary critic, critic, polemicist\n- Concepts: existentialism, Western theatre, culture, politics\n\nFacts:\n- George Bernard Shaw was born on 26 July 1856 and died on 2 November 1950.\n- George Bernard Shaw insisted on being known simply as Bernard Shaw.\n- George Bernard Shaw was an Irish playwright, critic, and polemicist whose influence on Western theatre, culture, and politics extended from the 1880s through his death and beyond.\n- Jean-Paul Sartre was born on 21 June 1905 and died on 15 April 1980.\n- Jean-Paul Sartre was a French philosopher, playwright, novelist, political activist, biographer, and literary critic.\n- Nausea is a philosophical novel by the existentialist philosopher Jean-Paul Sartre.\n- Nausea was published in 1938.\n- Nausea is titled La Nausée in French.",
